    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/0DB1CFB7BAA1AF7EF9E6616BC163C95A/jobs/247146": {
      "title": "Set Up Custodian",
      "description": "Set Up Custodian You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Set Up Custodian Sweet Briar College - Sweet Briar, VA 24595 Apply Overview Level Entry Position Type Full Time Job Shift Day Education Level High School Diploma or completed GED Travel Percentage None Category Facilities Apply Housekeeper/Custodian Job Title: Set Up Custodian Classification: Non-exempt Reports To: Housekeeping Supervisor Job Summary/Objective: The purpose of this position is to assist in the set up for campus events and physical movement of campus resources. The Set-Up Custodian position will interact with students, employees and guests and will need to have a keen customer service acumen. This position is integral to the success of the college. Position Type/Expected Work Hours: Full time, Monday –Friday 7 am -3:30 pm, some evening/weekend availability/Overtime will be required. Supervisory Responsibilities: None Essential Responsibilities: Set up of tables, chairs etc. for various campus events and communicate well with stakeholders Break down any equipment, furniture, etc. after campus events as needed Monitor inventory of tables, chairs, canopies etc. Perform stripping and waxing of VCT floors Daily recycling collection from campus proper and apartments/homes Cleaning of various floors with mechanical equipment Adjust, clean and maintain specialty equipment including floor scrubbers, carpet cleaning machine, etc. Cleaning of campus vehicle fleet Mopping VCT tile floors, hardwood floors, tile floors, marble floors, and stairwells Distribution of supplies to academic, residential and administrative buildings Empty and clean trash and recycling receptacles, Wash interior and exterior windows, glass doors, and mirrors Must handle various cleaning solvents and chemicals in the correct way set forth by supervisor, OSHA regulations, EPA, State Health Department, etc. Work effectively as part of housekeeping team Move heavy furniture, supplies, and different equipment when needed Able to climb and use 6’ and 8’ ladders Complete work orders assigned by supervisor in a timely manner Willingness to learn mechanical operation of housekeeping equipment, become van certified and offer support/assistance to other team members Qualifications Required Qualifications: High School Diploma or equivalent Experience in use of mechanical cleaning equipment Requires general knowledge of cleaning terms and safety procedures related to hazardous chemicals Ability to interpret set up diagrams Ability to read, write and follow oral and written instructions Must be well organized and able to prioritize work Ability to drive a pick-up truck with lift gate Clean MVR Preferred Qualifications: Experience in hospitality or comparable customer service position Work Environment: Work is both indoors and outdoors. Must be prepared to work in both environments’ year round Physical Demands: Extended periods of standing/walking are required, ability to lift 50+ lbs., moving 96-gallon recycling carts stooping/kneeling/climbing step ladders are required. Travel: None Other Duties: This job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee. Other duties, responsibilities and activities may change or be assigned at any time with or without notice. The hourly range for this position is $16.00-17.00 per hour. This is commensurate with education and experience and will be determined in accordance with institutional guidelines. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
