    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/0DB1CFB7BAA1AF7EF9E6616BC163C95A/jobs/245760": {
      "title": "Senior Admissions Recruiter",
      "description": "Senior Admissions Recruiter You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Senior Admissions Recruiter Sweet Briar College - Sweet Briar, VA 24595 Apply Overview Level Experienced Position Type Full Time Education Level 4 Year Degree Category Admin - Clerical Apply Description About Sweet Briar College Sweet Briar College is a nationally recognized liberal arts institution committed to cultivating female leaders. Consistently ranked among the most innovative liberal arts colleges by U.S. News & World Report, Sweet Briar stands out for its robust liberal arts programs and unique opportunities in women’s leadership, engineering, sustainability, the arts, and its renowned equestrian program. Nestled in the foothills of Virginia’s Blue Ridge Mountains, our picturesque campus features stunning lakes, forests, trails, vineyards, and greenhouses. With an intimate student-to-faculty ratio of 8:1, Sweet Briar fosters close-knit, supportive relationships that empower students to thrive academically and personally. Job Summary Sweet Briar College is seeking an experienced, results-oriented Senior Admissions Counselor to join the Department of Enrollment Management. This position plays a key role in recruiting, engaging, and enrolling prospective students while managing an assigned recruitment territory and student portfolio from initial inquiry through enrollment. The Senior Admissions Counselor is expected to bring demonstrated experience in college admissions, strong relationship-building and consultative recruitment skills, sound judgment, and a data-informed approach to territory and pipeline management. In addition to carrying an individual recruitment portfolio, this role will serve as an experienced resource to colleagues, contribute to counselor training and best-practice sharing, and help strengthen the overall effectiveness of the Admissions team. Qualifications Position Type / Expected Work Hours This is a full-time, onsite position, Monday through Friday, with regular flexibility required for recruitment travel, campus programs, evening and weekend events, and other enrollment activities. This is not a remote or hybrid position. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution. Minimum of three years of progressively responsible experience in college admissions, enrollment management, student recruitment, or a closely related higher education function. Demonstrated success managing a recruitment territory, student portfolio, admissions funnel, or comparable enrollment goals. Strong understanding of the college recruitment and admissions process, including prospect development, application completion, yield, and enrollment conversion. Experience using a CRM or student recruitment platform to manage communication, activity, and pipeline performance; experience with Slate is strongly preferred. Exceptional oral and written communication, presentation, and relationship-building skills. Ability to interpret enrollment data, identify trends, prioritize outreach, and adjust recruitment strategies based on results. Strong organizational skills and the ability to manage competing priorities, deadlines, travel, and a high-volume student portfolio. Demonstrated ability to work independently while contributing positively to a collaborative, results-focused team environment. Ability and willingness to coach, mentor, and share effective practices with less-experienced team members. Valid driver’s license and ability to meet College requirements for operating a motor vehicle. Commitment to educating and empowering young women and to advancing Sweet Briar College’s mission and long-term success. Preferred Qualifications Four or more years of college admissions or enrollment recruitment experience. Experience with Slate CRM. Experience recruiting for a private liberal arts college, women’s college, or similarly high-touch residential institution. Experience developing yield strategies, using enrollment analytics, training admissions staff, or leading recruitment initiatives. Work Environment Primarily office-based when not traveling, with regular movement across campus and occasional outdoor exposure during events. Evening and weekend work is required periodically based on recruitment travel and event schedules. Physical Demands Prolonged periods of computer use and regular walking across campus and recruitment venues. Ability to lift and transport recruitment materials weighing up to 20 pounds. Travel Regular seasonal travel is required for assigned recruitment territories, college fairs, school visits, outreach programs, and professional development. Overnight and occasional weekend travel should be expected during peak recruitment periods. Other Duties This job description is intended to describe the general nature and level of work performed and is not an exhaustive list of all responsibilities. Duties may evolve or expand based on departmental and institutional needs. Salary Range $55,000–$65,000 annually, commensurate with experience and qualifications. Application Process Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. To apply, please submit a cover letter and resume. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
